AUDIT_REPORT.md, Medium: "CSV/PDF export — neither exists anywhere."

PDF is the browser's own Print dialog (PrintButton + @media print CSS)
rather than a server-rendered file, added to the Ads report (admin,
client portal, and public share page), Shopify report (admin + client
portal), and the Clients list (admin).

CSV is Route Handlers, not client-side blobs: /api/export/campaigns
(admin), /client/export/campaigns (client portal — lives under /client/*
because the session cookie is path-scoped there), and /api/export/clients
(admin-only roster). Each surface resolves workspaceId through its own
existing auth exactly as its page does, never a query param, to keep this
from becoming a cross-tenant export hole. Public share links get Print
but not CSV.

An adversarial review pass before shipping caught and fixed two real
bugs: unvalidated since/until could crash the route via a CRLF-in-header
error (now rejected with a 400), and campaign/contact names starting
with =+-@ could execute as spreadsheet formulas on open (CSV/formula
injection, CWE-1236) — now neutralized with a leading apostrophe.

Extracted clients/page.tsx's page-local shopTotals/inline-filter into
shared, exported crm/queries.ts functions so the roster page and its CSV
export can never silently drift apart.

